    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Malicious .docx with injected settings.xml.rels written to user Temp", "technique": "T1221", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-17 09:18:10 UTC, Sysmon EID 11 captured creation of C:\\Users\\e.aboubakar\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p123_091810\\corp_q3_report.docx by powershell.exe. Static-scan of the embedded settings.xml.rels reveals Type='...attachedTemplate' AND Target='http://198.51.100.42/evil.dotx' AND TargetMode='External'. Marker score 4/4. Rule 92200 triggered.", "chain_reason": "A .docx whose settings.xml.rels references an external HTTP URL via TargetMode=External has zero legitimate use. Corp templates use local relative paths ('../templates/Normal.dotm') — never external HTTP."},
